<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jam Rawal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1562</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jam Rawal was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadeja">Jadeja</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> chief from Kutch who founded the state of Nawanagar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>. Around 1540 he conquered the Halar region and founded the town of Nawanagar, the 'new town', later called Jamnagar after the dynasty's title of Jam. His kinsmen founded other Jadeja states in the region, including Dhrol, established by his brother Hardholji.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jam-rawal.jpg" alt="Jam Rawal" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rangilo Gujarati · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jam_Raval.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
